<title>USA: CWM sees loss from accounting treatment.</title>
<headline>CWM sees loss from accounting treatment.</headline>
<dateline>PASADENA, Calif. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>CWM Mortgage Holdings Inc said it was informed by the Securities and Exchange Commission that its planned merger with Countrywide Asset Management Corp (CAMC) should be accounted for as a settlement of a contract, rather than a business combination.</p>
<p>CWM said it intends to conform with this recommendation, which it expects to result in &quot;a reported loss during the quarter in which the transaction settles.&quot;</p>
<p>As a result, the transaction will have a one-time rather than long-term effect on the earnings, CWM said.</p>
</text>
